        "en" to GemDetails(
            "NWA 7034, nicknamed “Black Beauty”, is a Martian breccia: a rock formed on the surface of Mars by the clumping together of fragments of different rocks, cemented by impacts and volcanic processes. It contains fragments dated to about 4.4 billion years, among the oldest pieces of Martian crust known. About 5 to 10 million years ago, an asteroid impact on Mars blasted this block into space; after a long journey, it fell to Earth, in the Sahara, at an unknown date. In 2022 its probable source crater, Karratha, was identified in the Terra Cimmeria region.",
